set of degradation precedes the other?\", \"allowed_tools\": [\"query_metrics\"], \"filters\": {\"start_ts\": \"2026-10-01T11:50:00Z\", \"end_ts\": \"2026-10-01T12:30:00Z\", \"services\": [\"gateway\", \"backend\"]}, \"reason\": \"Gateway 5xx is observed but gateway depends on backend, so latency/error onset ordering between the two is needed to distinguish an upstream origin from a downstream victim.\", \"expected_discriminator\": \"If backend latency/error rises at or before gateway's, backend is the propagation origin; if backend only degrades after gateway, gateway or a shared downstream dependency is implicated instead.\"}, {\"task_id\": \"task-metrics-0003\", \"role\": \"database\", \"question\": \"For postgres within 2026-10-01T11:50:00Z to 2026-10-01T12:30:00Z, do active connections, lock waits, or slow queries change before backend/gateway degrade?\", \"allowed_tools\": [\"get_db_connections\", \"get_db_active_sessions\", \"get_db_lock_waits\", \"get_db_slow_queries\", \"get_db_health_metrics\"], \"filters\": {\"start_ts\": \"2026-10-01T11:50:00Z\", \"end_ts\": \"2026-10-01T12:30:00Z\", \"services\": [\"postgres\"]}, \"reason\": \"Backend depends on postgres and the observation window shows only downstream gateway errors; postgres-side connection, lock, and slow-query signals are needed to test the connection-exhaustion hypothesis and establish causal chronology.\", \"expected_discriminator\": \"Escalating postgres connections/lock waits or a slow-query burst preceding backend degradation supports postgres as origin, whereas stable postgres health shifts the origin to backend resources.\"}, {\"task_id\": \"task-changes-0003\", \"role\": \"changes\", \"question\": \"Were any other deployment, config, maintenance or scaling changes applied to gateway, backend, postgres, redis or payment in the observation window 2026-10-01T11:50:00Z to 2026-10-01T12:30:00Z beyond the runtime-1 backend runtime settings change?\", \"allowed_tools\": [\"query_changes\", \"get_config_diff\"], \"filters\": {\"start_ts\": \"2026-10-01T11:50:00Z\", \"end_ts\": \"2026-10-01T12:30:00Z\"}, \"reason\": \"The observed record set is limited to a single backend configuration change; exhaustive discovery of additional changes in the window is needed to exclude other change-driven mechanisms and to confirm the runtime-1 change is the sole relevant one.\", \"expected_discriminator\": \"Additional changes to gateway, postgres, redis or payment in the window would indicate alternative change-driven mechanisms; none found beyond runtime-1 leaves backend_pool_config_regression as the only config-driven candidate.\"}, {\"task_id\": \"task-changes-0004\", \"role\": \"changes\", \"question\": \"What is the complete config diff for the observed change runtime-1 applied to backend at 2026-10-01T12:00:10Z?\", \"allowed_tools\": [\"get_config_diff\"], \"filters\": {\"change_id\": \"runtime-1\"}, \"reason\": \"A change_id in metadata.change_id (runtime-1) is present on the observed change record; fetching its full diff confirms whether the pool-sizing regression is the only altered setting or part of a wider config change.\", \"expected_discriminator\": \"A diff confined to db_pool_max (20->2) with unchanged concurrency supports a targeted pool-sizing regression, whereas a broader multi-setting regression would point to a wider backend configuration regression.\"}, {\"task_id\": \"task-logs-0004\", \"role\": \"logs\", \"question\": \"Within 2026-10-01T11:50:00Z to 2026-10-01T12:30:00Z, do backend log entries contain connection-pool acquisition queuing or timeout phrasing at or after 2026-10-01T12:00:10Z, distinct from generic CPU or memory pressure messages?\", \"allowed_tools\": [\"query_logs\"], \"filters\": {\"start_ts\": \"2026-10-01T11:50:00Z\", \"end_ts\": \"2026-10-01T12:30:00Z\", \"service\": \"backend\"}, \"reason\": \"Omitting severity and contains on the first inspection prevents hidden observations; pool acquisition text appearing at or after the runtime-1 change discriminates backend_pool_config_regression from generic resource saturation.\", \"expected_discriminator\": \"Connection-pool acquisition timeout or queuing entries beginning at or after 2026-10-01T12:00:10Z support backend_pool_config_regression; only generic resource-pressure messages instead point to backend_resource_saturation.\"}, {\"task_id\": \"task-metrics-0004\", \"role\": \"metrics\", \"question\": \"During 2026-10-01T11:50:00Z to 2026-10-01T12:30:00Z, do backend resource metrics show CPU or memory saturation coincident with the runtime-1 change, and do connection-pool utilization or acquisition-wait metrics change at or after 2026-10-01T12:00:10Z?\", \"allowed_tools\": [\"query_metrics\"], \"filters\": {\"start_ts\": \"2026-10-01T11:50:00Z\", \"end_ts\": \"2026-10-01T12:30:00Z\", \"service\": \"backend\"}, \"reason\": \"Resource metrics provide the independent signal needed to separate pool-acquisition queuing from generic resource saturation, since the observed log excerpt alone does not discriminate them.\", \"expected_discriminator\": \"A rise in pool acquisition-wait or utilization at or after 2026-10-01T12:00:10Z without matching CPU/memory saturation supports backend_pool_config_regression; coincident CPU or memory saturation instead supports backend_resource_saturation.\"}, {\"task_id\": \"task-db-0004-01\", \"role\": \"database\", \"question\": \"Between 2026-10-01T11:50:00Z and 2026-10-01T12:30:00Z, what are backend database connection counts, active sessions, and lock waits, and do they saturate before 2026-10-01T12:00:10Z?\", \"allowed_tools\": [\"get_db_connections\", \"get_db_active_sessions\", \"get_db_lock_waits\", \"get_db_health_metrics\"], \"filters\": {\"start_ts\": \"2026-10-01T11:50:00Z\", \"end_ts\": \"2026-10-01T12:30:00Z\", \"services\": [\"backend\"]}, \"reason\": \"Backend pool_waiters=118 at 12:00:10Z suggests connection-pool pressure; database-side connection and session metrics would discriminate connection exhaustion from lock contention or slow-query causes.\", \"expected_discriminator\": \"Database connection counts at or near the pool limit with elevated active sessions supports postgres_connection_exhaustion; dominant lock waits or slow queries would instead point to lock contention or slow_query.\"}, {\"task_id\": \"task-metrics-0004-02\", \"role\": \"metrics\", \"question\": \"Between 2026-10-01T11:50:00Z and 2026-10-01T12:30:00Z, what are the backend request_latency_ms, pool_waiters, and error-rate time series values, and do they begin rising strictly before 2026-10-01T12:00:00Z?\", \"allowed_tools\": [\"query_metrics\"], \"filters\": {\"start_ts\": \"2026-10-01T11:50:00Z\", \"end_ts\": \"2026-10-01T12:30:00Z\", \"services\": [\"backend\"]}, \"reason\": \"Current backend evidence is limited to single-point snapshots at 12:00:00Z and 12:00:10Z; a full time series is needed to establish the true onset of backend degradation relative to the gateway 5xx symptom.\", \"expected_discriminator\": \"A backend latency/pool_waiters rise beginning before 2026-10-01T12:00:00Z confirms backend as the propagation origin; onset at or after the gateway 5xx observation would shift the origin elsewhere.\"}, {\"task_id\": \"task-db-0006\", \"role\": \"database\", \"question\": \"Between 2026-10-01T11:50:00Z and 2026-10-01T12:30:00Z, do postgres active sessions, lock waits, or slow queries show sustained anomalies that could cause the backend and gateway degradation?\", \"allowed_tools\": [\"get_db_active_sessions\", \"get_db_lock_waits\", \"get_db_slow_queries\", \"get_db_health_metrics\", \"get_db_connections\"], \"filters\": {\"start_ts\": \"2026-10-01T11:50:00Z\", \"end_ts\": \"2026-10-01T12:30:00Z\", \"service\": \"postgres\"}, \"reason\": \"postgres-level contention or slow-query mechanisms require measured blocking sessions or long query durations to be viable; if absent while capacity is healthy, database-level causes are refuted.\", \"expected_discriminator\": \"Dominant lock waits or slow queries would support postgres_lock_contention or postgres_slow_query; their absence combined with healthy connection capacity refutes database-level causes.\"}, {\"task_id\": \"task-metrics-0006\", \"role\": \"metrics\", \"question\": \"Between 2026-10-01T11:50:00Z and 2026-10-01T12:30:00Z, does backend's database connection count stay pinned at or below the reduced db_pool_max of 2 while pool_waiters remains high?\", \"allowed_tools\": [\"get_metrics\"], \"filters\": {\"start_ts\": \"2026-10-01T11:50:00Z\", \"end_ts\": \"2026-10-01T12:30:00Z\", \"service\": \"backend\"}, \"reason\": \"The reduced db_pool_max bound is the decisive discriminator for backend_pool_config_regression; only backend pool telemetry can confirm the cap and the accompanying waiter behaviour.\", \"expected_discriminator\": \"Backend connection count pinned at 2 with high pool_waiters supports backend_pool_config_regression; backend connections below the bound without waiters refutes it.\"}, {\"task_id\": \"task-metrics-0007\", \"role\": \"metrics\", \"question\": \"For postgres between 2026-10-01T11:50:00Z and 2026-10-01T12:30:00Z, what metric names are actually available (discover with empty metric_names) and what are their connection-utilization, active-connection and error time series?\", \"allowed_tools\": [\"query_metrics\"], \"filters\": {\"service\": \"postgres\", \"start_ts\": \"2026-10-01T11:50:00Z\", \"end_ts\": \"2026-10-01T12:30:00Z\", \"metric_names\": []}, \"reason\": \"The postgres metric scope currently rests on one snapshot; discovering the real metric names and pulling their time series is required to test whether the dependency saturates or stays healthy.\", \"expected_discriminator\": \"A rising utilization or error series that leads backend degradation supports a postgres-side origin; a flat, healthy postgres series while backend pool_waiters is elevated supports the backend-internal pool regression mechanism.\"}, {\"task_id\": \"task-database-0007\", \"role\": \"database\", \"question\": \"For postgres between 2026-10-01T11:50:00Z and 2026-10-01T12:30:00Z, what do db connections, active sessions, lock waits, slow queries and health metrics show, and do any change before backend and gateway degrade?\", \"allowed_tools\": [\"get_db_connections\", \"get_db_active_sessions\", \"get_db_lock_waits\", \"get_db_slow_queries\", \"get_db_health_metrics\"], \"filters\": {\"service\": \"postgres\", \"start_ts\": \"2026-10-01T11:50:00Z\", \"end_ts\": \"2026-10-01T12:30:00Z\"}, \"reason\": \"The connection metric snapshot alone cannot separate connection exhaustion from lock contention or slow queries on the postgres side.\", \"expected_discriminator\": \"Saturated sessions or lock waits/slow queries on postgres preceding backend degradation point to a postgres-side mechanism; healthy postgres sessions with elevated backend pool_waiters point to the backend pool configuration regression.\"}], \"completed_task_ids\": [\"task-metrics-0001\", \"task-changes-0002\", \"task-logs-0003\", \"task-metrics-0004\", \"task-db-0005\", \"task-metrics-0006\"], \"tool_calls_used\": 10, \"llm_calls_used\": 15, \"tokens_used\": 0, \"incident_alert\": null, \"task_records\": [], \"workflow_status\": \"RUNNING\", \"termination\": null, \"variant\": \"dynamic_no_verifier\", \"benchmark_rca\": true, \"workflow_profile\": \"legacy_rca\", \"database_enabled\": true, \"role_tool_acl\": {\"database\": [\"get_db_connections\", \"get_db_active_sessions\", \"get_db_lock_waits\", \"get_db_slow_queries\", \"get_db_health_metrics\"], \"coordinator\": [], \"monitoring\": [], \"remediation\": [], \"logs\": [\"query_logs\"], \"metrics\": [\"query_metrics\", \"get_dependencies\", \"get_db_connections\", \"get_db_active_sessions\", \"get_db_lock_waits\", \"get_db_slow_queries\", \"get_db_health_metrics\"], \"changes\": [\"query_changes\", \"get_config_diff\"], \"verifier\": [\"fetch_evidence_by_ids\"], \"reporter\": [\"fetch_evidence_by_ids\"], \"single\": [\"query_logs